# M6 · 6.1.1 — build the Rust graph (MMTk + the GC binding) for size. The GC static archive is
# embedded in nomuc and linked into every emitted program, so its code size is a direct floor on
# every Nomu binary. `-Copt-level=z` cut a hello-world from ~15.6 MB (opt-level=0) to ~2.8 MB (with
# the driver's `-dead_strip`). Applies to Rust only; C++/Swift/LLVM keep their compilation_mode, so
# LLVM/Swift stay cached for fast iteration.
#
# Tradeoff: `z` optimizes for size over speed. When M6 turns to GC throughput (6.3), revisit — a
# faster level (`s`/`2`) on the collector hot path may be worth the size.
build --@rules_rust//rust/settings:extra_rustc_flags=-Copt-level=z
